# Checks and layout

`npm test` at the repo root is the definition of done. It runs every workspace, including the dependency-direction check. `npm run build` must succeed. A failing check does not ship.

Stack: Vite 6, vanilla JS ES modules, KaTeX 0.16, three.js 0.172 for 3D labs. No framework and no TypeScript build. JSDoc on `defineCourse`, `defineLab`, and `problem`. Tests are `node --test` scripts.

The hub dev server is port 5173. Leave 5174–5179 for the course apps: PHY 5174, MAC 2313 5175, Statics 5176, STA 3032 5177, MAC 2311 5178, MAC 2312 5179.

Mobile first. Design at 380px portrait, and check 1280px too. No horizontal scroll. `npm run smoke` opens the hub in headless Chrome at both widths and follows each course card to its live app.

TeX in a JS string is a `String.raw` template. A backslash eaten by an ordinary string is a failing tex-check once that course is in the repo.

Deploy is a Cloudflare Pages direct upload (`npm run deploy` to project `flux-study`). Pushing `main` does not publish the hub.
